o segments, Food and Support Services United States, and Food and Support Services International. It offers food-related managed services, including dining, catering, food service management, and convenience-oriented retail services; non-clinical food and food-related support services, such as patient food and nutrition, retail food, environmental services, and procurement services; and plant operations and maintenance, custodial/housekeeping, energy management, grounds keeping, and capital project management services. The company also provides on-site restaurants, catering, convenience stores, and executive dining services; beverage and vending services; and facility management services comprising landscaping, transportation, capital program management, payment services, and other facility consulting services relating to building operations. In addition, it offers concessions, banquet, and catering services; retail services and merchandise sale, recreational, and lodging services; and facility management services at sports, entertainment, and recreational facilities. Further, the company offers correctional food; and operates commissaries, laundry facilities, and property rooms. The company was formerly known as ARAMARK Holdings Corporation. Aramark was founded in 1959 and is based in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania.","ceo_bio":"Mr. John J. Zillmer | CEO & Director | Age 70 | Compensation: $4.9M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 278K people. Revenue per employee of $66K ranks in the bottom quartile among Industrials peers. Each employee generates $2K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $211 per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 73\u00d7 revenue per employee (elevated relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Aramark is a large-cap industrials business with a $14.2B market cap on $18.5B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +4% over the past three years and +3% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 6% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $432M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 2 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.82\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.7\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and thin 2.2\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 1.7%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.4\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $4.3M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-4310717.78},{"text":"Significant goodwill (37% of assets) from past acquisitions \u2014 a soft asset a conservative appraisal discounts to zero","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 6% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","12 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Earnings Outlook Improves Might Change The Case For Investing In Aramark Stock (ARMK)","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/consumer-services/nyse-armk/aramark/news/earnings-outlook-improves-might-change-the-case-for-investin-2","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794483334.838,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.872,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance"]},{"title":"Investment Analysts\u2019 Price Target Changes for November 11th (AHR, AMBQ, ANF, ARMK, AZTA, BRX, CF, COLD, CTRE, DOC)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/11/investment-analysts-price-target-changes-for-november-11th-ahr-ambq-anf-armk-azta-brx-cf-cold-ctre-doc.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794433493.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.557,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"Seeking Clues to Aramark (ARMK) Q4 Earnings? A Peek Into Wall Street Projections for Key Metrics","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/seeking-clues-aramark-armk-q4-202316289.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794428596.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.44,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Aramark $ARMK